{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I had a fever last night—101.7—and I’ve been feeling worse this morning with congestion and a headache. I’ve had a cough and stuffiness for a couple months, but this felt like a new wave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And any pain when you urinate or increased urgency?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. But my urine test at the clinic showed something abnormal, so they sent me here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Given your history of kidney transplant and diabetes, we take fevers seriously. We’ve started you on an IV antibiotic called cefepime to cover possible infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Is it a UTI? I’ve had those before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Your urine showed white blood cells, which suggests infection. We sent a culture to confirm. But your symptoms could also be from sinusitis—especially with this ‘second sickening’ after a period of improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t have yellow or green mucus. Just pressure in my forehead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. Bacterial sinusitis doesn’t always produce discharge. We’re treating it empirically because of your transplant and the fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. What about my kidney? I’m worried about rejection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound. The transplant looks structurally normal—no blockage or fluid. But the blood flow resistance is slightly higher than before. It’s not alarming, but we’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. And my chest X-ray? I’ve had radiation changes before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it shows old radiation fibrosis, but no new pneumonia. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My blood sugars have been high—339 this morning. Is that from the infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Illness raises blood sugar. We’re not changing your insulin pump yet, but we’ll keep an eye on it. Your team will see you tomorrow to adjust if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using my Humalog pump as usual. But I switched to Novolog in the discharge plan—why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s the same type of insulin—rapid-acting. The hospital uses Novolog, so we’re aligning your discharge plan with what’s available. You can switch back if needed, but they’re very similar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I see I’m on cefpodoxime now. Is that instead of the IV antibiotic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The urine culture grew E. coli, and it’s sensitive to cefpodoxime. It covers both the UTI and sinusitis. You’ll take it twice daily for 13 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to penicillin. Is this safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Cefpodoxime is a cephalosporin. There’s a small cross-reactivity risk, but it’s generally safe in penicillin-allergic patients, especially since your allergies are to amoxicillin and doxycycline. We’ll watch for any reaction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I also see I’m back on my statin. Was it stopped?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We hold statins in the hospital when you’re on cyclosporine because together they can increase the risk of muscle damage. But your cardiologist’s note says you’ve tolerated it before, so it’s safe to restart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had some leg cramps. Could that be from the statin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Let us know if they worsen. We may need to adjust the dose or switch medications. Also, you mentioned you sometimes miss your cilostazol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I forget sometimes. It’s one of many pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But cilostazol helps with circulation, especially with your diabetes and vascular disease. Missing doses can increase risk of clots. A pill organizer might help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a good idea. I’ll get one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We also checked your cyclosporine level this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And? Is it okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2188-04-24 15:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 65, which is a bit low. But you said you didn’t take your morning dose, so we won’t adjust it today. Just make sure to take it consistently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2188-04-24 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be more careful. I didn’t realize it affects the level so much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2188-04-24 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It does. Consistent dosing is key to preventing rejection. We’ll reinforce that with your transplant team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2188-04-24 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the nasal spray I was given?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2188-04-24 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Oxymetazoline—just for three days. It helps congestion, but longer use can make it worse. After that, use the fluticasone nasal spray daily for inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2188-04-24 16:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No more than three days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve been doing well—afebrile since admission. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Are the blood and urine cultures back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The urine culture confirmed E. coli, sensitive to your antibiotic. Blood cultures are still pending, but you’re stable, so we can safely discharge with oral treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve moved up your nephrology and endocrine appointments. You’ll see them within the next week. Call if you develop fever, pain, or high blood sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and finish all your antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I monitor my temperature at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially the first few days. If it goes above 100.4, or you feel worse, come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, keep checking your blood sugar four times a day as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have my logbook with me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Bring that to your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and get some rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with your prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for her."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Feel free to call the clinic with any questions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2188-04-25 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2188-04-24 14:54:00",
